= Abstract

#set par(justify: true)

This project aims to develop a structured and curated peptide database by resolving unknown amino acids and expanding incomplete functional annotations in UniProt peptide sequences. The study will combine external peptide databases, literature verification, and UniRef cluster information to improve sequence quality and annotation reliability. Machine learning models will then be used to study how ambiguous sequence information affects peptide function prediction. The project will also develop uncertainty-aware prediction methods to improve prediction reliability under incomplete data conditions. The expected outcome is a high quality peptide resource that supports more accurate and reliable AI-based peptide discovery and function prediction.